# Alpaca SMA20 Minute Scalper

## Source
- Source citation: 2026 URL reference, `alpacahq/example-scalping` README and `main.py`, https://github.com/alpacahq/example-scalping
- Source: [[sources/github-topic-algorithmic-trading-python]]
- Topic URL: https://github.com/topics/algorithmic-trading?l=python
- Repository: `alpacahq/example-scalping`, institution `Alpaca`
- Repo URL: https://github.com/alpacahq/example-scalping
- README: https://github.com/alpacahq/example-scalping/blob/master/README.md
- Strategy file: https://github.com/alpacahq/example-scalping/blob/master/main.py

## Mechanics

### Entry
- Timeframe: M1 bars, completed-bar evaluation.
- Calculate SMA(20) of close using current session bars.
- Open long when prior close is below prior SMA(20) and current close crosses above current SMA(20).
- Source is long-only stock scalping; V5 port tests long-only first on liquid DWX indices and FX majors. Target symbols: EURUSD.DWX, GBPUSD.DWX, NDX.DWX, SP500.DWX backtest-only.

### Exit
- Immediately after buy fill, submit a sell limit at `max(entry_price + one tick, current_price)`.
- Cancel unfilled buy orders after 2 minutes.
- Force-close any open position at 15:55 New York time in the source; V5 should use configured session-end flatten for the tested DWX venue.

### Stop Loss
- Source explicitly says risk control can be improved and leaves sell orders outstanding. V5 build should add a catastrophic stop of `1.5 * ATR(14)` on M1 or a max 0.35% adverse move, whichever is tighter after symbol normalization.

### Position Sizing
- Source uses a fixed dollar `lot` per symbol. V5 baseline uses fixed $1,000 risk per trade and one position per magic.

### Additional filters
- Trade only during liquid sessions; skip Friday close window and major news blackout.
- Use limit entries; if market has moved more than 0.3% from signal close before entry, skip.

